From 1f3ff04f098c3361ad2d502c1d0060242ac44ee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:44:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: reach StringRef::starts_with in llvmjit_inline

`llvm::StringRef::startswith` was renamed to `starts_with` in LLVM 16 and
removed outright in LLVM 18, so compiling the LLVM JIT against LLVM 18 or newer
fails in `llvmjit_inline.cpp`:

    error: no member named 'startswith' in 'llvm::StringRef';
    did you mean 'starts_with'?

Babelfish 4.0 forks PostgreSQL 16.1, one release short of the 16.2 that reaches
the new name and defines it back to the old one for LLVM older than 16, so one
source serves every LLVM the branch supports. This is that change, carried into
the fork. Babelfish 5.1 forks 17.4 and has it already.

The `#define` is function-local, matching upstream: this is the only call site,
and nothing else in the translation unit spells either name.

References: https://postgr.es/c/60ba7cae7c
---
 src/backend/jit/llvm/llvmjit_inline.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/jit/llvm/llvmjit_inline.cpp b/src/backend/jit/llvm/llvmjit_inline.cpp
index c765add856..6db25fa5cd 100644
--- a/src/backend/jit/llvm/llvmjit_inline.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/jit/llvm/llvmjit_inline.cpp
@@ -808,7 +808,10 @@ static void
 add_module_to_inline_search_path(InlineSearchPath& searchpath, llvm::StringRef modpath)
 {
 	/* only extension in libdir are candidates for inlining for now */
-	if (!modpath.startswith("$libdir/"))
+#if LLVM_VERSION_MAJOR < 16
+#define starts_with startswith
+#endif
+	if (!modpath.starts_with("$libdir/"))
 		return;
 
 	/* if there's no match, attempt to load */
